  <p>
    Fleet maintenance means the same tracking problem as a single vehicle, multiplied across however many are on
    the road. Missing one MOT or service date in a fleet of twenty is easy when it's tracked on a spreadsheet;
    GarageCloud's <a href="/features/mot-reminders">reminders</a> track every vehicle automatically, whether that's
    five vehicles or fifty — part of what <a href="/garage-management-software">garage management software</a> covers.
  </p>

  <h2>What fleet work needs that single-vehicle work doesn't</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Reminders that scale — every vehicle tracked individually, not one shared due-date list.</li>
    <li>Courtesy car tracking, since fleet customers need vehicles kept moving while one is in for work.</li>
    <li>Consolidated invoicing per fleet account, not per individual vehicle.</li>
    <li>A job history per vehicle that a fleet manager can review on request, tracked on the same <a href="/features/workshop-board">workshop board</a> as everything else.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Keeping a fleet account organised</h2>
  <p>
    A fleet customer is usually one invoicing relationship covering many vehicles and many jobs. GarageCloud keeps
    that structure — one account, multiple vehicles, a shared history — rather than treating each vehicle as an
    unrelated customer that happens to share a name. See <a href="/pricing">pricing</a> for which plan fits.
  </p>
